    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\n\r\nI am really enjoying mini.pick but would like to ask a question:\r\n\r\nWould you be opposed to introduce a not operator/modifier like fzf has?\r\nBasically like the `'` for an exact match, but all entries that do match are filtered out.\r\nI would propose to also use `!` for this. \r\n\r\nIf you are ok with this would you rather implement this yourself or are you open to a pull request for this?\r\n\r\nGreetings\r\nStefan",
