        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Oh I would be totally fine with your way, I actually think it is more consistent. What I like about it is, that it should make the implementation actually quite straight forward in that instead of filtering non matches out you only keep the non matching.\r\n\r\nIn the simplest form though not the most performant we could simply remove the matches of the current methods from the original list.\r\n\r\nIf you still don't like it that is also totally fine for me, I don't want to push you into something you don't like. In that case I will just implement it for myself on top of `MiniPick.default_match`\r\n",
